Swift's concerts are equipped with elaborate settings, incorporating elements from [[Broadway theatre]] and [[high tech]].<ref>{{cite news |last=O'Connor |first=Roisin |date=June 8, 2018 |title=Taylor Swift 'Reputation' Stadium Tour Review: Dazzling Pop Spectacle From the Star Who Doesn't Stand Still |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/reviews/taylor-swift-reputation-tour-review-manchester-a8390456.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220526/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/reviews/taylor-swift-reputation-tour-review-manchester-a8390456.html |archive-date=June 30, 2023 |access-date=December 22, 2019 |newspaper=[[The Independent]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Savage |first=Mark |date=March 18, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Launches Eras Tour with Three-Hour, 44-Song Set |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-64999388 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230318212358/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-64999388 |archive-date=March 18, 2023 |access-date=March 18, 2023 |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Sisario |first=Ben |author-link=Ben Sisario |date=November 5, 2023 |title=How Taylor Swift's Eras Tour Conquered the World |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/05/arts/music/taylor-swift-eras-tour.html |url-access=limited |access-date=August 12, 2023 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]] |archive-date=August 5, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230805093722/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/05/arts/music/taylor-swift-eras-tour.html/ |url-status=live}}</ref> She does not rely on elaborate choreography and instead emphasizes connecting emotionally with her audience through storytelling and vocal delivery.<ref>{{cite news |last=Seibert |first=Brian |date=August 9, 2023 |title=How to Command a Stage Without Great Dance Moves (Taylor's Version) |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/09/arts/dance/taylor-swift-eras-tour-dancing.html |url-access=limited |access-date=August 11, 2023 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]] |archive-date=August 22, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230822024623/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/09/arts/dance/taylor-swift-eras-tour-dancing.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Since 2007, she has toured with the same live band.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Procell |first1=Carlie |last2=Padilla |first2=Ramon |date=April 28, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Tour Has Many 'Eras'. We Tracked Her Movements to Give You the Look and Feel. |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/graphics/2023/04/27/taylor-swift-movements-eras-tour/11696828002/ |access-date=June 30, 2023 |newspaper=[[USA Today]]}}</ref> She plays four instruments live: guitar (including [[Electric guitar|electric]], acoustic six-string, and [[Twelve-string guitar|twelve-string]]), six-string banjo, piano, and [[ukulele]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 19, 2013 |title=Behind the Scenes at a Taylor Swift Concert |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/behind-the-scenes-at-a-taylor-swift-concert/ |access-date=July 22, 2025 |publisher=[[CBS News]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mah |first=Emmelyn |date=July 7, 2025 |title=Taylor Swift and Her Custom Guitar and Piano Collection, As Seen on the Eras Tour |url=https://www.prestigeonline.com/sg/lifestyle/culture-plus-entertainment/taylor-swift-guitar-piano-collection-eras-tour-gibson/ |access-date=July 22, 2025 |website=[[Prestige Hong Kong]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Lewis |first=Randy |date=April 3, 2011 |title=Academy of Country Music Awards: Las Vegas Welcomes Miranda Lambert, Taylor Swift with Open Arms |url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/blogs/awards-tracker/story/2011-04-03/academy-of-country-music-awards-las-vegas-welcomes-miranda-lambert-taylor-swift-with-open-arms |url-access=limited |access-date=August 20, 2023 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]]}}</ref>

Critics have praised her stage presence, stamina,<ref>{{cite news |last=Horton |first=Adrian |date=March 18, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Review – Pop's Hardest-Working Star Gives Eras Tour Her All |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/mar/18/taylor-swift-eras-tour-review-arizona |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230318140036/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/mar/18/taylor-swift-eras-tour-review-arizona |archive-date=March 18, 2023 |access-date=March 18, 2023 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Kaplan |first=Ilana |date=March 18, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift's 'Eras' Tour Is a Thrilling Spectacle From a Pop Mastermind |url=https://inews.co.uk/culture/taylor-swift-the-eras-tour-glendale-arizona-review-a-thrilling-spectacle-from-a-pop-mastermind-2217091 |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230318215357/https://inews.co.uk/culture/taylor-swift-the-eras-tour-glendale-arizona-review-a-thrilling-spectacle-from-a-pop-mastermind-2217091 |archive-date=March 18, 2023 |access-date=March 18, 2023 |newspaper=[[The i Paper]]}}</ref> and ability to bring forth an intimate atmosphere for her audience, even in stadium settings.<ref name="Petrusich-2023" /><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Krelenstein |first=Greg |date=May 21, 2018 |title=Taylor Swift's Reputation Tour Is a Pop Triumph |url=https://vmagazine.com/article/taylor-swifts-reputation-tour-is-a-pop-triumph/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180522111614/https://vmagazine.com/article/taylor-swifts-reputation-tour-is-a-pop-triumph/ |archive-date=May 22, 2018 |access-date=May 22, 2018 |magazine=[[V (American magazine)|V]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Kornhaber |first=Spencer |date=March 18, 2023 |title=What Made Taylor Swift's Concert Unbelievable |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/culture/archive/2023/03/taylor-swift-eras-tour-review/673438/ |url-access=subscription |access-date=June 30, 2023 |website=[[The Atlantic]]}}</ref> [[Sasha Frere-Jones]], in a 2008 article for ''[[The New Yorker]]'', hailed her as a "preternaturally skilled" entertainer who exerted professionalism with a vibrant energy.<ref name="Jones-2008" /> In ''Time''{{'s}} 2023 [[Time Person of the Year|Person of the Year]] piece, [[Sam Lansky]] wrote: "Swift is many things onstage—vulnerable and triumphant, playful and sad—but the intimacy of her songcraft is front and center."<ref name="Lansky-2023" />

=== Videos and filmmaking ===
Swift emphasizes visuals as a key creative component of her music.<ref name="Ordoña-2022">{{cite news |last=Ordoña |first=Michael |date=September 9, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift Wants an Oscar. So She Took 'All Too Well' to TIFF |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2022-09-09/taylor-swift-tiff-oscar-all-too-well-toronto-2022 |url-access=limited |access-date=September 10, 2022 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]]}}</ref> She established her production company, [[Taylor Swift Productions]], in 2008.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Fulwood |first=Alice |date=July 24, 2024 |title=How to Get Rich (Taylor's Version) |url=https://www.economist.com/1843/2024/07/24/how-to-get-rich-taylors-version |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240901111552/https://www.economist.com/1843/2024/07/24/how-to-get-rich-taylors-version |archive-date=September 1, 2024 |access-date=September 2, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Economist]]}}</ref> Her directorial debut was the music video for "Mine", co-directed with [[Roman White]], in 2010;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Dailey |first=Hannah |date=October 25, 2022 |title=Here Are All of Taylor Swift's Self-Directed Music Videos, From 'All Too Well' to 'Bejeweled' |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/taylor-swift-music-videos-she-directed-herself/ |access-date=July 23, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> and she developed the concept and [[Film treatment|treatment]] for "Mean" in 2011.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 4, 2011 |title=Taylor Swift's 'Mean' Video Debuts Friday |url=http://www.cmt.com/news/1663245/taylor-swifts-mean-video-debuts-friday/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190619161133/http://www.cmt.com/news/1663245/taylor-swifts-mean-video-debuts-friday/ |archive-date=June 19, 2019 |access-date=June 19, 2019 |publisher=[[CMT (American TV channel)|CMT]]}}</ref> For the music videos of the ''1989'' and ''Reputation'' singles, she collaborated extensively with the director [[Joseph Kahn (director)|Joseph Kahn]] on eight videos;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Hé |first=Kristen S. |date=March 12, 2018 |title=Taylor Swift's 'Delicate' Video Dances Away Her Regrets: Critic's Take |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/taylor-swift-delicate-video-analysis-dancing-reputaiton-8240727/ |access-date=July 23, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> among them, she produced "Bad Blood", which won [[Best Music Video]] at the Grammy Awards in 2016.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wagmeister |first=Elizabeth |date=May 18, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift Debuts Star-Packed 'Bad Blood' Music Video |url=https://variety.com/2015/music/awards/bad-blood-taylor-swift-watch-music-video-1201498985/ |access-date=July 23, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> She worked with [[American Express]] for the "Blank Space" music video (which Kahn directed) and served as executive producer for the interactive app ''AMEX Unstaged: Taylor Swift Experience'', for which she won a [[Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Interactive Program]] in 2015.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=O'Connell |first=Michael |date=October 9, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift and Jimmy Fallon Among Early Emmy Winners |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/taylor-swift-wins-emmy-interactive-821735 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190619164926/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/taylor-swift-wins-emmy-interactive-821735 |archive-date=June 19, 2019 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

As of February&nbsp;2026, Swift has [[Taylor Swift videography|directed 15 of her music videos]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gularte |first=Alejandra |date=May 2, 2025 |title=So, What Happened With Taylor Swift's Directorial Debut? |url=https://www.vulture.com/article/taylor-swift-directorial-debut-explained.html |url-access=limited |access-date=July 23, 2025 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]}}</ref> Her first solo directorial role was for "The Man", which made her the first female artist to win the [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Direction]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lynch |first=Jessica |date=August 31, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Tells Fans: 'You Are the Only Reason the Industry Cares' |url=https://au.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-vmas-2020-16334/ |access-date=July 23, 2025 |website=[[Rolling Stone Australia]]}}</ref> ''All Too Well: The Short Film'' marked her filmmaking debut,<ref name="Dailey-2022" /> and it made her the first artist to win the Grammy Award for Best Music Video as a solo director.<ref>{{cite web |last=Weatherby |first=Taylor |date=February 5, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Makes Grammy History (Again) With Best Music Video Win For ''All Too Well: The Short Film'' |url=https://www.grammy.com/news/taylor-swift-all-too-well-the-short-film-best-music-video-winner-2023-grammys |access-date=February 6, 2023 |publisher=[[National Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences]]}}</ref> In June&nbsp;2023, Swift was invited to the [[Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Blistein |first=Jon |date=June 28, 2023 |title=Aspiring Filmmaker Taylor Swift Invited to Join Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/tv-movies/tv-movie-news/taylor-swift-invited-to-join-oscars-film-academy-1234780300/ |url-access=limited |access-date=July 23, 2025 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> She has cited Joseph Kahn, [[Chloé Zhao]], [[Greta Gerwig]], [[Nora Ephron]], [[Guillermo del Toro]], [[John Cassavetes]], and [[Noah Baumbach]] as filmmaking influences.<ref name="Ordoña-2022" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Coates |first=Lauren |date=September 20, 2022 |title=On The Rise of Taylor Swift, Filmmaker |url=https://www.rogerebert.com/features/on-the-rise-of-taylor-swift-filmmaker |access-date=July 23, 2025 |website=[[RogerEbert.com]]}}</ref>

