Swift has won 14 Grammy Awards, including a record four [[Grammy Award for Album of the Year|Album of the Year]] wins;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last1=Gibson |first1=Kelsie |last2=Krauser |first2=Emily |date=January 31, 2026 |title=How Many Grammys Does Taylor Swift Have? See Every Time She Won the Coveted Awards |url=https://people.com/how-many-grammys-does-taylor-swift-have-11896157 |access-date=April 23, 2026 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |archive-date=April 23, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260423175954/https://people.com/how-many-grammys-does-taylor-swift-have-11896157 |url-status=live }}</ref> she has also received a record eight nominations for [[Song of the Year]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Most Grammy Nominations for Song of the Year |url=https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/761579-most-grammy-nominations-for-song-of-the-year |access-date=April 23, 2026 |website=[[Guinness World Records]] |archive-date=March 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260304083055/https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/761579-most-grammy-nominations-for-song-of-the-year |url-status=live }}</ref> Swift has additionally won 12{{nbsp}}Country Music Association Awards,<ref name="Ryan-2017">{{cite web |last=Ryan |first=Patrick |date=November 9, 2017 |title=Taylor Swift, Pop Princess, Wins Song of the Year at the CMA Awards |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/entertainthis/2017/11/08/taylor-swift-pop-princess-wins-song-year-cma-awards/846929001/ |access-date=April 23, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]] |archive-date=August 20, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190820071255/https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/entertainthis/2017/11/08/taylor-swift-pop-princess-wins-song-year-cma-awards/846929001/ |url-status=live }}</ref> 8{{nbsp}}Academy of Country Music Awards,<ref>{{cite news |last=Zornosa |first=Laura |date=September 17, 2020 |title=There's No Place like Home: Taylor Swift Digs Up Her Country Roots at ACM Awards |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2020-09-17/taylor-swift-digs-her-country-roots-at-the-academy-of-country-music-awards |access-date=April 23, 2026 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]] |url-access=limited |archive-date=September 18, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200918020451/https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2020-09-17/taylor-swift-digs-her-country-roots-at-the-academy-of-country-music-awards |url-status=live }}</ref> 2{{nbsp}}[[Brit Awards]],<ref name="GlobalIcon">{{cite magazine |last=Mier |first=Tomás |date=May 11, 2021 |title=Taylor Swift Accepts Global Icon Award at 2021 Brits: Let 'Cynicism or Skepticism Fuel You' |url=https://people.com/music/taylor-swift-wins-global-icon-award-brits-2021/ |access-date=April 11, 2015 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |archive-date=June 13, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210613094323/https://people.com/music/taylor-swift-wins-global-icon-award-brits-2021/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and an [[Emmy Award]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last1=Friedlander |first1=Whitney |date=September 10, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift, Jimmy Fallon Among Juried Emmy Award Winners |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |url=https://variety.com/2015/tv/news/taylor-swift-jimmy-fallon-chris-hardwick-emmy-winners-1201589918/ |access-date=August 3, 2016 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150915095938/http://variety.com/2015/tv/news/taylor-swift-jimmy-fallon-chris-hardwick-emmy-winners-1201589918/ |archive-date=September 15, 2015}}</ref> She is the most-awarded artist of the American Music Awards (40 wins),<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Millman |first=Ethan |date=April 14, 2026 |title=Taylor Swift Leads 2026 American Music Awards With Eight Nominations |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/music/music-news/american-music-awards-2026-nominations-list-1236563285/ |access-date=April 23, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |archive-date=April 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260416035334/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/music/music-news/american-music-awards-2026-nominations-list-1236563285/ |url-status=live }}</ref> the [[Billboard Music Awards|''Billboard'' Music Awards]] (49),<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Grein |first=Paul |date=December 13, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Stands Alone as Billboard Music Awards' All-Time Top Winner After 10 New Wins |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/taylor-swift-billboard-music-awards-record-1235853360/ |access-date=December 14, 2024 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |archive-date=February 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260204111003/https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/taylor-swift-billboard-music-awards-record-1235853360/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and the MTV Video Music Awards (30, tied with [[Beyoncé]]).<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Grein |first=Paul |date=September 12, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Ties Beyoncé as All-Time Top VMAs Winner |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/taylor-swift-vmas-2024-passes-beyonce-top-winner-1235773005/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240926121613/https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/taylor-swift-vmas-2024-passes-beyonce-top-winner-1235773005/ |archive-date=September 26, 2024 |access-date=September 30, 2024 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> Swift is the first woman to be honored with the Pinnacle Award by the Country Music Association Awards in 2013 and with the Global Icon Award by the Brit Awards in 2021.<ref>{{cite news |last=Caramanica |first=Jon |author-link=Jon Caramanica |date=November 7, 2013 |title=Country Awards Hold Swift Close |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/arts/music/at-country-music-awards-swift-is-celebrated.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131111094215/http://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/arts/music/at-country-music-awards-swift-is-celebrated.html |archive-date=November 11, 2013 |access-date=April 3, 2014 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref><ref name="GlobalIcon" />

At the 64th [[BMI Pop Awards]] in 2016, Swift became the first female songwriter to be honored with an award named after its recipient.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Polanco |first=Luis |date=April 5, 2016 |title=Taylor Swift to Receive First-Ever Taylor Swift Award From BMI |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/bmi-pop-awards-taylor-swift-award-barry-mann-cynthia-weil-7325271/ |access-date=April 23, 2026 |archive-date=February 21, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260221052224/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/bmi-pop-awards-taylor-swift-award-barry-mann-cynthia-weil-7325271/ |url-status=live }}</ref> She is the youngest person to be featured on ''Rolling Stone''{{'s}} list "[[Rolling Stone's 100 Greatest Songwriters of All Time|The 100 Greatest Songwriters of All Time]]" (2015) and the youngest woman to be inducted into the [[Songwriters Hall of Fame]] (2026).<ref>{{cite magazine |title=The 100 Greatest Songwriters of All Time |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/100-greatest-songwriters#taylor-swift |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170902114756/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/100-greatest-songwriters#bob-dylan |archive-date=September 2, 2017 |access-date=August 28, 2017 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Mason |first1=Anthony |last2=Castagna |first2=Rebecca |last3=Earl |first3=Jennifer |last4=Fitzpatrick |first4=Meghan |date=January 21, 2026 |title=Taylor Swift Makes History As Songwriters Hall of Fame Inductee: See the Full Class of 2026 |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/taylor-swift-songwriters-hall-of-fame-inductees-full-list-2026/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260122063351/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/taylor-swift-songwriters-hall-of-fame-inductees-full-list-2026/ |archive-date=January 22, 2026 |access-date=January 21, 2026 |publisher=[[CBS News]]}}</ref> She received the Songwriter Icon Award from the [[National Music Publishers' Association]] in 2021 and was named the Songwriter-Artist of the Decade by the Nashville Songwriters Association International in 2022.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Eggertsen |first=Chris |date=June 9, 2021 |title=Taylor Swift Accepts NMPA Songwriter Icon Award, Thanks Her Songwriting 'Teachers' in Speech |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/taylor-swift-nmpa-songwriter-icon-award-speech/ |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |url-access=subscription |access-date=April 23, 2026 |archive-date=June 30, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250630163841/https://www.billboard.com/pro/taylor-swift-nmpa-songwriter-icon-award-speech/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Minsker |first=Evan |date=September 20, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift Named Songwriter-Artist of the Decade by NSAI: Read Her Speech |url=https://pitchfork.com/news/taylor-swift-named-songwriter-artist-of-the-decade-by-nsai-read-her-speech/ |website=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]] |access-date=April 23, 2026 |archive-date=January 2, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260102022128/https://pitchfork.com/news/taylor-swift-named-songwriter-artist-of-the-decade-by-nsai-read-her-speech/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The [[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry]] (IFPI) honored Swift as the [[Global Recording Artist of the Year]] six times (2014, 2019, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025), more than any other artist.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 18, 2026 |title=Taylor Swift named IFPI's Official Biggest-Selling Global Artist of the Year for a sixth time |url=https://www.ifpi.org/taylor-swift-named-ifpis-official-biggest-selling-global-artist-of-the-year-for-a-sixth-time/ |access-date=February 18, 2026 |publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry]] |archive-date=April 7, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260407151429/https://www.ifpi.org/taylor-swift-named-ifpis-official-biggest-selling-global-artist-of-the-year-for-a-sixth-time/ |url-status=live }}</ref> She is the most-streamed artist of all time on Spotify as of April&nbsp;2026,<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Aswad |first=Jem |date=April 23, 2026 |title=Spotify Reveals All-Time Most-Streamed Artists, Albums, Songs and More: Taylor Swift, Bad Bunny and the Weeknd Top Lists |url=https://variety.com/2026/music/news/spotify-lists-all-time-most-streamed-artists-albums-songs-taylor-swift-bad-bunny-weeknd-1236728433/ |access-date=April 23, 2026 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-date=April 23, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260423181816/https://variety.com/2026/music/news/spotify-lists-all-time-most-streamed-artists-albums-songs-taylor-swift-bad-bunny-weeknd-1236728433/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and the [[List of highest-grossing live music artists#All-time ranking|highest-grossing touring act of all time]], with cumulative revenue at $3.12&nbsp;billion as of December&nbsp;2024.<ref>Sources:
* {{Cite magazine |date=June 10, 2022 |title=Top Touring Artist of the Pollstar Era |url=https://data.pollstar.com/Chart/2022/07/072522_top.touring.artists_1020.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220805190603/https://data.pollstar.com/Chart/2022/07/072522_top.touring.artists_1020.pdf |archive-date=August 5, 2022 |access-date=August 4, 2022 |magazine=[[Pollstar]]}}
