status=live }}</ref> Swift is the first woman to have both an album and a song receive diamond certifications from the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA),<ref>{{cite web |last=Ahlgrim |first=Callie |date=November 15, 2025 |title=There Are 193 Songs in History That Have Been Certified Diamond — Here They All Are |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/every-diamond-certified-song-ever-riaa |access-date=April 23, 2026 |website=[[Business Insider]] |archive-date=March 2, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302052907/https://www.businessinsider.com/every-diamond-certified-song-ever-riaa |url-status=live }}</ref> and also to have 100 million RIAA-certified album units.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kaplan |first=Ilana |date=September 30, 2025 |url=https://people.com/taylor-swift-riaa-history-first-artist-100-million-album-sales-11821401 |title=Taylor Swift Makes RIAA History as First and Only Female Artist to Surpass 100 Million Album Sales |access-date=April 23, 2026 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |archive-date=December 20, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251220132204/https://people.com/taylor-swift-riaa-history-first-artist-100-million-album-sales-11821401 |url-status=live }}</ref> ''Billboard'' ranked Swift at number eight on its list "Greatest of All Time Artists" (2019),<ref>{{cite magazine |title=Greatest of All Time Artists |url=https://www.billboard.com/charts/greatest-of-all-time-artists |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191114170915/https://www.billboard.com/charts/greatest-of-all-time-artists |archive-date=November 14, 2019 |access-date=November 15, 2019 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> number three on "Top Country Artists of the 21st Century" (2025),<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Asker |first=Jim |date=May 27, 2025 |title=Kenny Chesney Is No. 1 on Billboard's Top Country Artists of the 21st Century Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/kenny-chesney-top-country-ar