== Public image ==
{{Main|Public image of Taylor Swift}}

[[File:5.3.10TaylorSwiftByDavidShankbone.jpg|thumb|upright=.7|Swift at the 2010 [[Time 100|''Time'' 100]] Gala|alt=Swift posing, wearing a black sleeveless cocktail dress and black earrings]]
Swift is an enduring figure of 21st-century [[popular culture]].{{Sfn|Franssen|2022|p=90}} Her career trajectory from a country singer-songwriter to a pop star in the 2000s and 2010s was the subject of extensive commentary.<ref name="Rosen-2013" />{{Sfn|McNutt|2020|p=79}} Deemed "America's Sweetheart" in her early career, she was described in the press as a "media darling" with a [[girl-next-door]]'s polite demeanor and open-hearted conversations.{{sfn|Fischer|Seidman|2016|p=529}}<ref name="Knibbs-2019">{{Cite web |last=Knibbs |first=Kate |date=August 21, 2019 |title=Ten Years of Taylor Swift: How the Pop Star Went From Sweetheart to Snake (and Back Again?) |url=https://www.theringer.com/2019/08/21/music/ten-years-of-taylor-swift |access-date=July 30, 2025 |website=[[The Ringer (website)|The Ringer]]}}</ref> Swift displayed a feminine image but refrained from the "aggressively sexualized feminist pop" of her contemporaries, leading publications to comment that her [[sex appeal]] was modest, subtle, and sophisticated.<ref name="Rosen-2013" /><ref>{{Cite news |last=Kessler |first=Zara |date=November 6, 2014 |title=Taylor Swift's Sexual Temptation |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/view/articles/2014-11-05/taylor-swift-s-sexual-temptation |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170729220348/https://www.bloomberg.com/view/articles/2014-11-05/taylor-swift-s-sexual-temptation |archive-date=July 29, 2017 |access-date=August 1, 2025 |publisher=[[Bloomberg L.P.]]}}</ref>{{Sfn|Brown|2012|p=176}} The adolescent themes of Swift's music contributed to her status as a [[teen idol]],<ref>{{cite news |date=November 2, 2012 |title=Taylor Swift: 'My Confidence Is Easy To Shake' |url=https://www.npr.org/2012/11/03/164186569/taylor-swift-my-confidence-is-easy-to-shake |access-date=May 20, 2021 |publisher=[[NPR]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Thanki |first=Juli |date=September 24, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift: Teen Idol to 'Biggest Pop Artist in the World' |url=https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2015/09/24/taylor-swift-teen-idol-biggest-pop-artist-world/72744548/ |access-date=May 13, 2021 |newspaper=[[The Tennessean]]}}</ref> although several [[feminist]] authors took issue with her songs about romantic relationships as narrow-minded and detrimental to girls and women, who made up the majority of her fanbase known as [[Swifties]].{{Sfnm|1a1=Brown|1y=2012|1pp=176–177|2a1=Finley|2y=2023|2p=494}}

Upon recalibrating her artistry to pop music, Swift has identified as a feminist and achieved a [[pop icon]] status.<ref name="Levine-2019" /><ref name="Knibbs-2019" /> In 2013, the author [[Jody Rosen]] labelled Swift the "Queen of Pop", citing her popularity that defied traditional boundaries between "genres, eras, demographics, paradigms, trends".<ref name="Rosen-2013" /> Her feminist public image garnered varied reactions from the public, including praise for her success in a male-dominated music industry as an inspiration for girls and women, and criticism that dismissed her feminist adoption as superficial and self-interested.{{Sfn|Finley|2023|p=494}}

The 2016 dispute with Kanye West bolstered the narrative among Swift's detractors that she was a calculating and manipulative woman despite her sweetheart image, and deepened [[Taylor Swift–Kanye West feud|their feud]] that has resonated in their respective careers.{{Sfn|Cullen|2016|p=33}}<ref>{{cite web |last1=Grady |first1=Constance |date=August 26, 2019 |title=How the Taylor Swift-Kanye West VMAs Scandal Became a Perfect American Morality Tale |url=https://www.vox.com/culture/2019/8/26/20828559/taylor-swift-kanye-west-2009-mtv-vmas-explained |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251113175037/https://www.vox.com/culture/2019/8/26/20828559/taylor-swift-kanye-west-2009-mtv-vmas-explained |archive-date=November 13, 2025 |access-date=October 12, 2023 |website=[[Vox (website)|Vox]]}}</ref> Her artistic reinventions in the 2020s turned her into an acclaimed singer-songwriter.<ref name="Snapes-2022" /> Buoyed by her enduring pop stardom, she has been recognized as a rare phenomenon that combines the pop star and singer-songwriter archetypes with unprecedented success.<ref name="Sanders-2022" />{{Sfn|Hibbett|2022|p=25}} Swift is a known [[Triskaidekaphobia#Lucky 13|triskaidekaphile]], known for using the number [[13 (number)|13]] in her various works.<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 18, 2024 |title=The full history of Taylor Swift and her 'lucky number' 13 |url=https://www.today.com/popculture/music/taylor-swift-number-13-rcna129522 |access-date=October 6, 2025 |website=Today}}</ref>

== Cultural impact ==
{{Main|Cultural impact of Taylor Swift}}

[[File:Taylor Swift wax figure (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright=0.7|left|alt=Wax figure of Swift in a white oxford shirt, black hotpants holding a guitar|Wax figure of Swift at [[Madame Tussauds Sydney]]]]
Swift is one of the few artists who have consistently sold millions of albums throughout two decades despite the industry decline in record sales after the [[album era]] ended.<ref>{{cite news |last=Jericho |first=Greg |author-link=Greg Jericho |date=October 28, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift's Incredible Success in Graphs – Who Can Blame Me for Being a Swiftie As a 50-Year-Old Man? |url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/29/taylor-swifts-incredible-success-in-graphs-who-can-blame-me-for-being-a-swiftie-as-a-50yo-man |access-date=October 29, 2022 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Zoladz |first=Lindsay |date=December 30, 2019 |title=What Were the 2010s? |url=https://www.vulture.com/2019/12/taylor-swift-in-the-2010s.html |url-access=limited |access-date=November 22, 2020 |magazine=[[New York (magazine)|New York]]}}</ref> In this regard, academics and journalists have described her as "the last pop superstar" and "the last great rock star" of the 21st century.{{Sfn|Fogarty|Arnold|2021|p=3}}<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Cragg |first=Michael |date=October 28, 2022 |title=Is Taylor Swift Our Last Remaining Real Popstar? |url=https://i-d.co/article/how-did-taylor-swift-get-successful/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230506085436/https://i-d.vice.com/en/article/qjkakb/how-did-taylor-swift-get-successful |archive-date=May 6, 2023 |access-date=December 3, 2022 |magazine=[[i-D]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Nicolaou |first=Anna |date=October 27, 2022 |title=Is Taylor Swift the Last Pop Superstar? |url=https://www.ft.com/content/9cd1cd39-d4f5-45cd-8b72-24a1882b010b |url-access=subscription |access-date=July 30, 2025 |website=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref> Her commercial strategies to bolster sales of albums and concert tickets have earned her a reputation as a savvy businesswoman.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Lutz |first=Ashley |date=October 8, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift's New Album Proves She Is a Business Genius |url=https://fortune.com/2022/10/08/taylor-swift-midnights-release-business-strategy/ |url-access=subscription |access-date=October 8, 2022 |magazine=[[Fortune (magazine)|Fortune]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Brooks |first=Dave |date=November 3, 2022 |title=How Taylor Swift Changed the Course of the Concert Ticketing Businesses |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/taylor-swift-tours-changed-concert-ticket-sales/ |access-date=November 4, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Steele |first=Anne |date=July 1, 2023 |title=How to Succeed in Business Like Taylor Swift |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-to-succeed-in-business-like-taylor-swift-8165be7c |url-access=subscription |access-date=July 2, 2023 |newspaper=[[The Wall Street Journal]]}}</ref> The economist [[Alan Krueger]] described Swift as an "economic genius".<ref>{{cite news |last=Savaira |first=Augusta |date=November 23, 2022 |title=Welcome to 'Swiftonomics': What Taylor Swift Reveals About the U.S. Economy |url=https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2022-11-23/what-taylor-swift-reveals-about-us-economy |url-access=limited |access-date=November 23, 2022 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]]}}</ref> Strategies such as enhanced material for physical album variants and [[Easter egg (media)|easter egg]] usage in her works became indicative of music marketing trends.{{Sfn|Perone|2017|p=24}}<ref>{{cite news |last=Kheraj |first=Alim |date=November 9, 2022 |title=The Curate's Easter egg: How Taylor Swift Turned Pop Into a Multiplayer Puzzle |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/nov/09/how-taylor-swift-turned-pop-into-a-multiplayer-puzzle |access-date=November 9, 2022 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>

Swift's success in country music has been credited with popularizing the genre beyond the US and introducing it to adolescent women, a previously ignored demographic.<ref name="Rosen-2013" /><ref>{{cite news |last=Crummy |first=Colin |date=March 13, 2014 |title=Detwanging Country Music: How Nashville Took the UK |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2014/mar/13/country-music-taylor-swift-nashville-radio-2 |access-date=September 23, 2021 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref name="Roland-2016">{{cite magazine |last=Roland |first=Tom |date=July 7, 2016 |title=Love Story: The Impact of Taylor Swift's First Decade in Music |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/taylor-swift-music-career-ten-years-impact-country/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160714142858/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/country/7430895/taylor-swift-music-career-ten-years-impact-country |archive-date=July 14, 2016 |access-date=July 7, 2016 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The critic [[Kelefa Sanneh]] dubbed Swift the biggest country star since Garth Brooks, "and maybe since before him, too".{{Sfn|Sanneh|2021|p=190}} Her guitar performances resulted in increasing sales of guitars to women, which the media dubbed the "Taylor Swift factor".<ref>{{cite news |last1=O'Connor |first1=Roisin |date=October 18, 2018 |title=Half of All New Guitar Players Are Women, Finds Study |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/new-guitar-players-women-men-gender-split-fender-taylor-swift-a8589786.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220526/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/new-guitar-players-women-men-gender-split-fender-taylor-swift-a8589786.html |archive-date=May 26, 2022 |access-date=October 20, 2020 |newspaper=[[The Independent]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Wang |first1=Amy X. |date=May 22, 2018 |title=Guitars Are Getting More Popular. So Why Do We Think They're Dying? |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/pro/news/guitars-are-getting-more-popular-so-why-do-we-think-theyre-dying-630446/ |url-access=limited |access-date=October 20, 2020 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> Her transition from country to pop has been credited as the catalyst for poptimism,<ref>{{cite news |last=Gormely |first=Ian |date=December 3, 2014 |title=Taylor Swift Leads Poptimism's Rebirth |url=http://www.theguardian.com/music/2014/dec/03/taylor-swift-poptimism |access-date=August 2, 2021 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> and her songwriting and musical transitions have been credited with influencing a new generation of artists.<ref name="Hyden-2021" /><ref name="Roland-2016" /><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Schneider |first=Marc |date=October 30, 2023 |title=9 Ways Taylor Swift Has Changed the Music Business |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/how-taylor-swift-changed-music-business/taylor-swift-artists-rights/ |access-date=July 30, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> According to ''Billboard'', Swift is one of the few artists who can achieve chart success, critical acclaim, and fan support at the same time,<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=March 23, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift's 40 Biggest Hot 100 Hits |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/top-taylor-swift-songs-top-100-hits/ |access-date=April 12, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> and she has the ability to popularize any sound in mainstream music.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Lipshutz |first=Jason |date=December 16, 2021 |title=Billboard's Greatest Pop Stars of 2021: No. 1 — Taylor Swift |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/taylor-swift-greatest-pop-star-2021-1235011392/ |access-date=December 16, 2021 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref>

Swift's enduring popularity, particularly among female audiences, contributed to her status as a representation of [[millennials]],<ref>Sources:<br />{{*}} {{cite web |last=McDuling |first=John |date=November 3, 2014 |title=Why Taylor Swift Is the Most Important Artist of the Millennial Era |url=https://qz.com/290714/why-taylor-swift-is-the-most-important-artist-of-the-millennial-era/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602215053/https://qz.com/290714/why-taylor-swift-is-the-most-important-artist-of-the-millennial-era/ |archive-date=June 2, 2021 |access-date=April 2, 2021 |work=[[Quartz (publication)|Quartz]]}}<br />{{*}} {{cite news |date=October 6, 2015 |title=What Taylor Swift Tells Us about Millennials |url=https://nationalpost.com/entertainment/music/what-taylor-swift-tells-us-about-future-generations |access-date=October 30, 2021 |newspaper=[[National Post]]}}<br />{{*}} {{cite magazine |last=Kidd |first=Joel |date=March 2, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Is the Surprising Face of Millennial Anxiety |url=https://thewalrus.ca/taylor-swift-is-the-surprising-face-of-millennial-anxiety/ |access-date=October 30, 2021 |magazine=[[The Walrus]]}}<br />{{*}} {{cite news |last1=Winograd |first1=Morley |last2=D. Hais |first2=Michael |date=January 29, 2010 |title=Move Over Kanye West, Taylor Swift and the Millennial Generation Are Taking Over Music |url=https://www.csmonitor.com/Commentary/Opinion/2010/0129/Move-over-Kanye-West-Taylor-Swift-and-the-Millennial-generation-are-taking-over-music |access-date=October 30, 2021 |newspaper=[[The Christian Science Monitor]]}}<br />{{*}} {{cite news |date=October 21, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift Is Peak Millennial Vibes |url=https://www.npr.org/2022/10/19/1129868151/taylor-swift-is-peak-millennial-vibes |access-date=December 19, 2022 |publisher=[[NPR]]}}</ref> or, more broadly, of her generation's ''[[zeitgeist]]''.{{Sfn|Fogarty|Arnold|2021|p=6}}<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Bartsch |first=Kayla |date=September 24, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift: Empress of the Zeitgeist |url=https://www.nationalreview.com/2023/09/taylor-swift-empress-of-the-zeitgeist/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230927233053/https://www.nationalreview.com/2023/09/taylor-swift-empress-of-the-zeitgeist/ |archive-date=September 27, 2023 |access-date=September 24, 2023 |magazine=[[National Review]]}}</ref> Her fandom of Swifties has been described by journalists and academics as one of the most loyal and dedicated.<ref>{{cite web |last=Khan |first=Fawzia |date=June 18, 2021 |title=The Might Of Taylor Swift |url=https://elle.in/article/the-might-of-taylor-swift/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210628043313/https://elle.in/article/the-might-of-taylor-swift/ |archive-date=June 28, 2021 |access-date=October 20, 2021 |magazine=[[Elle (magazine)|Elle]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Djajapranata |first=Cliff |date=July 7, 2023 |title=The Linguistic Phenomenon Behind Taylor Swift's Superstardom |url=https://www.georgetown.edu/news/the-linguistic-phenomenon-behind-taylor-swifts-superstardom/ |access-date=August 1, 2025 |publisher=[[Georgetown University]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Zimmerman |first=Andrew |date=July 16, 2025 |title=There's a Formula to Loyalty—Super-Fandoms Have Mastered It |url=https://www.fastcompany.com/91368842/theres-a-formula-to-loyalty-super-fandoms-have-mastered-it |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250720155028/https://www.fastcompany.com/91368842/theres-a-formula-to-loyalty-super-fandoms-have-mastered-it |archive-date=July 20, 2025 |access-date=August 1, 2025 |magazine=[[Fast Company]]}}</ref> In the view of ''Time''{{'}}s Cady Lang, she maintained her superstardom through her "savvy manipulation of both the industry and [her] personal brand".<ref>{{Cite magazine |last1=Berman |first1=Judy |last2=Dockterman |first2=Eliana |last3=Gajanan |first3=Mahita |last4=Gutterman |first4=Annabel |last5=Lang |first5=Cady |date=September 3, 2021 |title=Sally Rooney and the Art of the Millennial Novel |url=https://time.com/6094903/sally-rooney-millennial-novel/ |url-access=limited |access-date=August 1, 2025 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] }}{{Dead link|date=April 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> According to the popular-culture scholars Mary Fogarty and [[Gina Arnold]], Swift is arguably the singular artist "whose story encapsulates many of the urgent conflicts in early twenty-first-century American culture".{{Sfn|Fogarty|Arnold|2021|pp=5–6}} In a 2024 article for ''[[The New York Times]]'', Joe Coscarelli wrote that her lasting popularity provoked debates comparing her not only to contemporaries like [[Drake (musician)|Drake]] or Beyoncé, but also to veteran artists like [[the Beatles]], [[Michael Jackson]], [[Elton John]], or Madonna.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Coscarelli |first1=Joe |last2=Cox |first2=Courtney |last3=Bierman |first3=Fred |date=May 17, 2024 |title=How Big Is Taylor Swift? |url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/05/17/arts/music/taylor-swift-sales-tours-grammys.html |url-access=registration |access-date=July 30, 2025 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref>

Swift's advocacy for artists' rights and re-recording projects have contributed to industry-wide discourses and reforms.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Sutherland |first=Mark |date=December 13, 2019 |title='I Come with Opinions About How We Can Better Our Industry': Taylor Swift |url=https://www.musicweek.com/interviews/read/i-come-with-opinions-about-how-we-can-better-our-industry-taylor-swift-the-music-week-interview/077961 |access-date=April 27, 2020 |magazine=[[Music Week]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Rosseinsky |first=Katie |date=October 29, 2021 |title=How Taylor Swift Is Changing the Music Industry a Re-Record At a Time |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/insider/taylor-swift-rerecording-albums-masters-fearless-b928211.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210409085520/https://www.standard.co.uk/insider/taylor-swift-rerecording-albums-masters-fearless-b928211.html |archive-date=April 9, 2021 |access-date=April 23, 2021 |newspaper=[[Evening Standard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Smith |first=Neil |date=June 22, 2015 |title=Five Ways Taylor Swift Is Changing the World |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-33222489 |access-date=December 31, 2019 |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> Her artistry and career maneuvers have been the subject of various university courses in literary, cultural, and [[sociopolitical]] contexts.{{sfn|Franssen|2022|p=90}}<ref>{{Cite web |last=Portugal |first=Adrian |date=February 29, 2024 |title=Another University Has Launched a Taylor Swift Course |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/asia/east-asia/taylor-swift-university-course-philippines-b2504638.html |access-date=August 1, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Independent]]}}</ref> According to the popular culture scholars Sarai Brinker, Kate Galloway, and Elizabeth Scala, Swift's legacy has been both embraced and critiqued by different affiliations—feminist and [[queer]] communities, [[far-right]] groups, and religious organizations, and studied by experts in various fields—musicology, literature, sociology, media theory, linguistics, and culture studies.<ref>{{Cite web |year=2025 |title=Submit a Manuscript to the Journal ''Popular Music and Society'': For a Special Issue on Taylor Swift |url=https://think.taylorandfrancis.com/special_issues/taylor-swift/ |access-date=August 1, 2025 |publisher=[[Taylor & Francis]] / [[Routledge]]}}</ref>

== Wealth and endorsements ==
Through her management company, TAS Rights Management, LLC, Swift has filed over 300 trademark applications in the US and holds more than 400 registrations worldwide, {{As of|2025|8|lc=y}}. Her filings include her name "Taylor Swift", her fanbase name "Swifties", album cover art and titles, tour names, lyrics, slogans, and her cats' names.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Caminero |first=Leticia |date=August 19, 2025 |title=Taylor Swift Trademark Strategy: A Model For Artist IP Protection |url=https://www.wipo.int/web/wipo-magazine/article-details/?assetRef=78728&title=taylor-swift-trademark-strategy-a-model-for-artist-ip-protection |access-date=September 9, 2025 |publisher=[[World Intellectual Property Organization]]}}</ref> Swift was listed by ''Forbes'' as the world's [[Forbes list of the world's highest-paid musicians|highest-paid musician]] in 2016 and 2019,<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Greenburg |first=Zack O'Malley |date=November 2, 2016 |title=Taylor Swift's Earnings: $170 Million In 2016 |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/zackomalleygreenburg/2016/11/02/taylor-swifts-earnings-170-million-in-2016/ |access-date=July 22, 2025 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=July 10, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift Named World's Highest Paid Celebrity |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2019/jul/10/taylor-swift-highest-paid-celebrity-list-kylie-jenner-kanye-west-lionel-messi-ronaldo |access-date=July 22, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> the highest-paid female musician of the 2010s decade,<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Greenburg |first=Zack O'Malley |date=December 23, 2019 |title=From Taylor Swift to Dr. Dre: The 10 Top-Earning Musicians of the Decade |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/zackomalleygreenburg/2019/12/23/from-beyonc-to-paul-mccartney-the-10-top-earning-musicians-of-the-decade/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191230220635/https://www.forbes.com/sites/zackomalleygreenburg/2019/12/23/from-beyonc-to-paul-mccartney-the-10-top-earning-musicians-of-the-decade/ |archive-date=December 30, 2019 |access-date=December 31, 2019 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> and the highest-paid female musician in 2021, 2022, and 2025.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Voytko |first=Lisette |date=February 9, 2022 |title=The Highest-Paid Entertainers 2022 |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/lisettevoytko/2022/02/09/the-highest-paid-entertainers-2022/ |access-date=July 29, 2022 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Voytko |first=Lisette |date=February 13, 2023 |title=The World's 10 Highest-Paid Entertainers |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/lisettevoytko/2023/02/13/the-worlds-top-10-highest-paid-entertainers-of-2022/?sh=71d0f4d129a3 |access-date=July 29, 2022 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Licosa |first=Martina Di |title=The Highest-Paid Musicians Of 2025 |date=December 30, 2025 |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/martinadilicosa/2025/12/30/the-highest-paid-musicians-of-2025/ |access-date=March 11, 2026 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref>

By October 2023, as reported by both ''[[Forbes]]'' and [[Bloomberg L.P.]], Swift had become a [[billionaire]]. She was recognized as the first billionaire "primarily based on her songs and performances", with the majority of her fortune coming from royalties and touring.<ref name="Forbes">{{Cite magazine |title=Taylor Swift ''Forbes'' Profile |url=https://www.forbes.com/profile/taylor-swift/ |access-date=August 2, 2025 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Ballentine |first1=Claire |last2=Pendleton |first2=Devon |last3=Sloan |first3=Dylan |date=May 30, 2025 |title=Taylor Swift Locked In Her Billionaire Status Before Acquiring Music |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-05-30/taylor-swift-s-billionaire-status-helped-her-reclaim-her-music-catalog |url-access=subscription |access-date=August 2, 2025 |publisher=[[Bloomberg L.P.]]}}</ref> {{As of|2026|3|df=US|post=,}} her estimated net worth by ''Forbes'' stands at $2 billion, making her the [[List of music artists by net worth|richest female musician in the world]]. The net worth of her music catalog is estimated at $900 million.<ref name="Forbes" /><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kaufman |first=Gil |date=October 7, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Passes Rihanna to Claim World's Richest Female Musician Crown With Est. $1.6B Net Worth |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/taylor-swift-passes-rihanna-worlds-richest-female-musician-billion-net-worth-1235794321/ |access-date=October 7, 2024 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> Her real estate portfolio, estimated by ''Forbes'' at $110&nbsp;million {{as of|2025|lc=on|post=,}}<ref name="Forbes" /> consists of residential properties in Nashville, New York City, Los Angeles ([[Samuel Goldwyn Estate]]), and [[Rhode Island]] ([[High Watch]]).<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Silva |first1=Rachel |last2=Tonelli |first2=Lucia |date=October 3, 2023 |title=Inside Taylor Swift's 8 Incredible Homes |url=https://www.elledecor.com/celebrity-style/celebrity-homes/g21792583/taylor-swift-house-home/ |access-date=October 12, 2023 |magazine=[[Elle (magazine)|Elle]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Sloan |first1=Kaycee |last2=Murphy |first2=Chad |date=February 9, 2025 |title=Where Does Taylor Swift Live? |url=https://www.cincinnati.com/story/entertainment/music/2025/02/09/where-does-taylor-swift-live/78182045007/ |access-date=August 2, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Cincinnati Enquirer]]}}</ref>

[[File:Taylor Swift for Keds.jpg|thumb|upright|alt=Side profile of Swift, dressed in a red jacket|Swift in a promotional video for [[Keds]] in 2015]]

Swift's use of [[private jet|private jets]] has drawn scrutiny for its [[carbon emissions]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Chiu |first=Allyson |date=August 3, 2022 |title=Celebrities Use Private Jets Excessively. It's a Climate Nightmare. |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/08/02/taylor-swift-kylie-jenner-private-jet-emissions/ |url-access=limited |access-date=February 14, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Mendez |first=Lola |date=February 14, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Claims She Offsets Her Travel Carbon Footprint – How Does That Work? |url=https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20240213-taylor-swift-private-jet-flight-travel-carbon-footprint |access-date=February 14, 2024 |publisher=[[BBC]]}}</ref> In 2023, a spokesperson for Swift stated that she had purchased more than double the required [[carbon credits]] to offset all tour travel and personal flights.<ref>{{cite news |last1=O'Malley |first1=Isabella |date=February 2, 2024 |title=Why Taylor Swift's Globe-Trotting in Private Jets Is Getting Scrutinized |url=https://apnews.com/article/taylor-swift-climate-jet-carbon-emissions-kelce-chiefs-02ac425d24281bd26d73bfdf4590bc82 |access-date=February 6, 2024 |work=[[Associated Press News]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=December 21, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift and Travis Kelce romance is bad for the planet. Couple burns a whopping $70,779 jet fuel in the last three months |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/us/taylor-swift-and-travis-kelce-romance-is-bad-for-the-planet-couple-burns-a-whopping-70779-jet-fuel-in-the-last-three-months/articleshow/106184435.cms |access-date=February 6, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Economic Times]]}}</ref> In December&nbsp;2023, Swift's lawyers sent a [[cease and desist]] letter to the American programmer [[Jack Sweeney]] for tracking her private jet, alleging stalking and safety risks. Media outlets have reported that the information posted by Sweeney is a synthesis of publicly available data.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Blistein |first1=Jon |date=February 6, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift's Lawyers Threaten Private Jet Flight Tracker Over 'Stalking and Harassing Behavior' |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swifts-lawyers-threaten-student-private-jet-tracker-1234962228/ |url-access=limited |access-date=February 6, 2024 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Matza |first=Max |date=February 7, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Threatens to Sue Student Who Tracks Her Private Jet |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-68223602 |access-date=February 7, 2024 |agency=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> In February 2024, it was reported that Swift had sold one of her two private jets.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kay |first1=Grace |last2=Rains |first2=Taylor |date=February 7, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Quietly Downsizes to One Private Jet |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/taylor-swift-gets-rid-of-one-private-jet-2024-2 |access-date=March 3, 2024 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref>

Swift's album rollouts typically consist of multimedia promotional activities that encompass corporate tie-ins and product endorsements.<ref>{{cite news |last=Curto |first=Justin |date=December 22, 2020 |title=Did 2020 Kill the Long, Fancy Pop-Album Rollout for Good? |url=https://www.vulture.com/2020/12/taylor-swift-evermore-folklore-surprise-explained.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201223023032/https://www.vulture.com/2020/12/taylor-swift-evermore-folklore-surprise-explained.html |archive-date=December 23, 2020 |access-date=December 27, 2020 |website=[[Vulture (magazine)|Vulture]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Leight |first=Elias |date=July 23, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Finally Abandoned the Traditional Album Rollout |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/taylor-swift-folklore-surprise-album-1033102/ |url-access=limited |access-date=September 15, 2022 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> [[Target Corporation|Target]] is a long-standing business partner with Swift, offering exclusive physical albums and merchandise.<ref name="Hampp-2011">{{cite magazine |last=Hampp |first=Andrew |date=December 10, 2011 |title=Women in Music 2011: Beyond Branding |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=jim-YANOn5AC&pg=RA11-PA32 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211025150235/https://books.google.com/books?id=jim-YANOn5AC&pg=RA11-PA32&lpg=RA11-PA32 |archive-date=October 25, 2021 |access-date=December 10, 2011 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |page=32 |via=[[Google Books]] |volume=123 |issue=35}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Chhith |first=Alex |date=October 15, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift, Target Partner for Exclusive Merch |url=https://www.startribune.com/target-taylor-swift-eras-tour-tortured-poet-department-exclusive-book-vinyl-black-friday/601162530 |url-access=subscription |access-date=August 2, 2025 |newspaper=[[Minnesota Star Tribune]]}}</ref> In 2008–2011, her albums and tours were promoted with self-designed dolls with [[Jakks Pacific]], fragrances with [[Elizabeth Arden, Inc.|Elizabeth Arden]], clothes with [[L.E.I.]], and holiday cards with [[American Greetings]].<ref name="Hampp-2011" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=November 9, 2008 |title=She's the New 'Got Milk' Girl |url=https://www.mcall.com/2008/11/09/shes-the-new-got-milk-girl/ |url-access=subscription |access-date=August 2, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Morning Call]]}}</ref> Her partnership deals included makeup products for [[CoverGirl]] and [[Cyber-shot]] cameras for [[Sony Electronics]].<ref name="Hampp-2011" /> In 2012–2015, she had tie-ins with [[Starbucks]], [[Keds]], [[Subway (restaurant)|Subway]], [[Diet Coke]], [[Walgreens]], [[Walmart]], and [[Papa John's]].<ref name="Lewis-2012" /><ref name="Christman-2014" />

In 2014, New York City named Swift its official tourism ambassador.{{Sfn|Busà|2017|p=203}} She had an exclusive streaming deal with Apple Music in 2015,<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Peoples |first=Glenn |date=December 14, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift's Partnership With Apple Is a Landmark — and Predictable — Deal |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-apple-music-1989-documentary-analysis-6806128/ |access-date=August 2, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> signed a multi-year deal with [[AT&T]] in 2016,<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=October 4, 2016 |title=Taylor Swift Signs Multi-Year Deal With AT&T, Will Headline Pre-Super Bowl Concert |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/taylor-swift-att-deal-super-bowl-saturday-concert/ |url-access=subscription |access-date=August 2, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> and partnered with [[United Parcel Service]] to distribute her albums in 2017.<ref name="Knibbs-2019" /> In 2019, Swift signed a multi-year deal with [[Capital One]] and launched a clothing line with [[Stella McCartney]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Lind |first=J. R. |date=May 15, 2025 |title=A Deal For The Eras: Capital One Charges In With Massive Taylor Swift Partnership |url=https://news.pollstar.com/2025/05/15/a-deal-for-the-eras-capital-one-charges-in-with-massive-taylor-swift-partnership/ |access-date=August 2, 2025 |magazine=[[Pollstar]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Coscarelli |first=Joe |date=August 23, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift Releases ''Lover'' the Old-Fashioned Way |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/23/arts/music/taylor-swift-lover.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190828234348/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/23/arts/music/taylor-swift-lover.html |archive-date=August 28, 2019 |access-date=September 1, 2019 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> She became the first global ambassador for [[Record Store Day]] in 2022.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kaufman |first=Gil |date=January 20, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift Tapped as First Record Store Day Global Ambassador |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/taylor-swift-2022-record-store-day-global-ambassador-1235020879/ |access-date=January 20, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref>

== Social activism ==
{{Further|Political impact of Taylor Swift}}

Swift avoided discussing politics in her early career.<ref name="Knibbs-2019" /> In a 2012 interview with ''Time'', she said that she kept herself as educated as possible but did not want to influence others with her political opinions.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Macsai |first=Dan |date=October 19, 2012 |title=Taylor Swift on Going Pop, Ignoring the Gossip and the Best (Worst) Nickname She's Ever Had |url=https://entertainment.time.com/2012/10/19/taylor-swift-on-going-pop-ignoring-the-gossip-and-the-best-worst-nickname-shes-ever-had/?iid=ent-main-lede |url-access=limited |access-date=August 3, 2025 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]}}</ref> Due to her apolitical stance, she was appropriated by the [[alt-right]] movement in the US, which sparked controversy.{{Sfn|Driessen|2022|p=1060}} She did express support for President [[Barack Obama]] in 2008: "I've never seen this country so happy about a political decision in my entire time of being alive."<ref name="Grigoriadis-2009" />

Since 2018, Swift has been public about her political views and has abandoned her once-apolitical stance.<ref name="Knibbs-2019" /><ref>{{cite news |last=Vincent |first=Alice |date=November 3, 2017 |title=Taylor Swift: The Rise, Fall and Re-Invention of America's Sweetheart |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/artists/taylor-swift-rise-fall-re-invention-americas-sweetheart/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220110/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/artists/taylor-swift-rise-fall-re-invention-americas-sweetheart/ |archive-date=January 10, 2022 |access-date=July 5, 2020 |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]]}}</ref> She publicly endorsed two [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] politicians for the [[2018 US midterm election]], which resulted in headlines about how she finally dissociated herself from the alt-right and [[Conservatism in the United States|conservatives]].{{Sfn|Driessen|2022|p=1060}} In interviews, she attributed her political reluctance in the past to the [[Dixie Chicks controversy|2003 Dixie Chicks controversy]], which left a lasting impact on country musicians at large and female country musicians in particular.{{Sfn|Moss|2022|p=45}} She has openly criticized President [[Donald Trump]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Schuster |first=Steve |date=May 19, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Comes Out Against Trump, Again |url=https://wislawjournal.com/2023/05/19/taylor-swift-comes-out-against-trump-again/ |access-date=November 4, 2023 |website=[[Wisconsin Law Journal]]}}</ref> In 2020, Swift urged her fans to check their voter registration ahead of elections, which resulted in 65,000 people registering to vote within one day of her post,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Haag |first1=Matthew |date=October 9, 2018 |title=Voter Registrations Spike as Deadlines Loom. Taylor Swift Had Something to Do With It. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/09/us/politics/taylor-swift-voter-registration.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181009210812/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/09/us/politics/taylor-swift-voter-registration.html |archive-date=October 9, 2018 |access-date=October 10, 2018 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> and endorsed the Democratic ticket of [[Joe Biden]] and [[Kamala Harris]] in the [[2020 US presidential election]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Stevens |first=Matt |date=October 7, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift, Leaning Further Into Politics, Endorses Joe Biden and Kamala Harris |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/07/us/politics/taylor-swift-joe-biden-kamala-harris.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201007230024/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/07/us/politics/taylor-swift-joe-biden-kamala-harris.html |archive-date=October 7, 2020 |access-date=October 8, 2020 |newspaper=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> For the [[2024 US presidential election|2024 election]], she once again endorsed the Democratic ticket of Harris and [[Tim Walz]].<ref>{{cite news |date=September 10, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Endorses Kamala Harris |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-rcna170547 |access-date=September 10, 2024 |publisher=[[NBC News]]}}</ref>

A [[pro-choice]] feminist,<ref name="Snapes-2019">{{cite news |last=Snapes |first=Laura |date=August 24, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift: 'Pop Music Can Feel like It's ''The Hunger Games'', And like We're Gladiators' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2019/aug/24/taylor-swift-pop-music-hunger-games-gladiators? |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190824114530/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2019/aug/24/taylor-swift-pop-music-hunger-games-gladiators |archive-date=August 24, 2019 |access-date=August 24, 2019 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref> Swift is a founding signatory of the [[Time's Up (organization)|Time's Up]] movement against sexual harassment,<ref>{{cite news |date=October 21, 2019 |title=The Original 300+ Time's Up Signatories |url=https://timesupnow.org/times-up-the-300-original-signatories/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200503222948/https://timesupnow.org/times-up-the-300-original-signatories/ |archive-date=May 3, 2020 |access-date=May 20, 2020 |publisher=[[Time's Up (organization)|Time's Up]]}}</ref> and she criticized the [[US Supreme Court]]'s [[Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization|decision to end federal abortion rights]] in 2022.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Mier |first=Tomás |date=June 24, 2022 |title=Taylor Swift Says She's 'Absolutely Terrified' After Roe v. Wade Decision |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-terrified-roe-v-wade-1373876/ |url-access=limited |access-date=June 24, 2022 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> A supporter of [[LGBTQ rights]], she has donated to the LGBT organizations [[Tennessee Equality Project]] and [[GLAAD]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Aniftos |first=Rania |date=April 8, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $113,000 to Tennessee Equality Project to Fight Anti-LGBTQ Bills |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/8506363/taylor-swift-donates-tennessee-equality-lgbtq |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190409102558/https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/8506363/taylor-swift-donates-tennessee-equality-lgbtq |archive-date=April 9, 2019 |access-date=April 9, 2019 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite press release |title=Taylor Swift Makes a Generous Donation to GLAAD in Support of the LGBTQ Community |date=June 1, 2019 |url=https://www.glaad.org/releases/taylor-swift-makes-generous-donation-glaad-support-lgbtq-community |access-date=June 1, 2019 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190601061137/https://www.glaad.org/releases/taylor-swift-makes-generous-donation-glaad-support-lgbtq-community |archive-date=June 1, 2019 |agency=[[GLAAD]]}}</ref> In 2019, she called for the passing of the [[Equality Act (United States)|Equality Act]] and performed during [[WorldPride NYC 2019]] at the [[Stonewall Inn]], a [[gay rights]] monument.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kreps |first=Daniel |date=June 1, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift Urges Senate to Pass Equality Act in Letter to Tennessee Senator |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-letter-lamar-alexander-equality-act-843155/ |url-access=limited |access-date=August 12, 2020 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Lynch |first=Joe |date=June 26, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Calls Out U.S. Census for Transgender Erasure |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/pride/9409947/taylor-swift-trans-erasure-census |access-date=June 29, 2020 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> Swift has spoken up against [[white supremacy]], racism, and [[Police brutality in the United States|police brutality]] in the US.<ref name="Hiatt-2019" /><ref name="Snapes-2019" /> She has supported the [[March for Our Lives]] movement and [[Gun politics in the United States|gun control reform]] in the US,<ref>{{cite news |last=Lynch |first=John |date=March 23, 2018 |title=Taylor Swift Shares Support For Gun a Control Reform In Instagram Post |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/taylor-swift-shares-support-for-gun-control-reform-in-instagram-post-2018-3 |access-date=May 20, 2020 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref> donated to the [[NAACP Legal Defense and Educational Fund]] and the [[Black Lives Matter]] movement,<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Bailey |first=Alyssa |date=June 9, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Tweeted About the Black Lives Matter Movement and Urged People to Vote |url=https://www.elle.com/culture/celebrities/a32815585/taylor-swift-black-lives-matter-voting-tweets/ |access-date=July 27, 2020 |magazine=[[Elle (magazine)|Elle]]}}</ref> called for the [[Removal of Confederate monuments and memorials|removal]] of [[Confederate States of America|Confederate]] monuments in Tennessee,<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Kreps |first=Daniel |date=June 12, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Calls for Removal of Monuments That 'Celebrate Racist Historical Figures' |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-tennessee-monuments-racist-historical-figures-removal-1014584/ |url-access=limited |access-date=August 12, 2020 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> and advocated for [[Juneteenth]] to become a national holiday.<ref>{{cite news |last=France |first=Lisa Respers |date=June 19, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Got Educated on Juneteenth and Wants You to Be, Too |url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/06/19/entertainment/taylor-swift-juneteenth/index.html |access-date=July 27, 2020 |publisher=[[CNN]]}}</ref>

Swift's political engagements have been met with mixed reception: they have provoked further public discussion of political issues and empowered Swifties, but critics have questioned whether her political alignments were strategic in her career.{{Sfnm|1a1=Fogarty|1a2=Arnold|1y=2021|1p=7|2a1=Driessen|2y=2022|2pp=1068–1069}} While some publications have argued that Swift's stardom had a significant impact on political involvement in the US, others have viewed her influence as sizable but overstated.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Laugier |first=Sandra |author-link=Sandra Laugier |date=September 20, 2024 |title='Taylor Swift Illustrates the Political Power of Popular Culture Through Her Support for Kamala Harris' |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2024/09/20/taylor-swift-illustrates-the-political-power-of-popular-culture-through-her-support-for-kamala-harris_6726685_23.html |access-date=August 3, 2025 |newspaper=[[Le Monde]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Veltman |first=Chloe |date=August 22, 2024 |title=Everyone Wants Taylor Swift's Vote. But Celebrity Endorsements Are Complicated. |url=https://www.npr.org/2024/08/22/nx-s1-5082376/celebrity-endorsements-of-presidential-nominees-complicated |access-date=August 3, 2025 |publisher=[[NPR]]}}</ref> According to the popular culture scholar Simone Driessen, her political impact extended beyond the US to Australia and Europe.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 1, 2024 |title=The Magic of Taylor Swift Unravelled |url=https://www.eur.nl/en/news/magic-taylor-swift-unravelled |access-date=August 3, 2025 |publisher=[[Erasmus University Rotterdam]]}}</ref>

== Philanthropy ==
Swift ranked first on [[DoSomething]]'s "Gone Good" list in 2012, 2013, 2014, and 2015.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Stutz |first=Colin |date=December 29, 2014 |title=Taylor Swift Tops DoSomething.org's 'Celebs Gone Good' List for Third Year in a Row |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-tops-dosomethingorgs-celebs-gone-good-list-for-third-year-in-a-6422346/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805075219/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-tops-dosomethingorgs-celebs-gone-good-list-for-third-year-in-a-6422346/ |archive-date=August 5, 2025 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Howard |first=Hanna |date=December 29, 2015 |title=Taylor Swift Was Just Named the Best Celebrity Do-Gooder |url=https://www.teenvogue.com/story/taylor-swift-tops-2015-celebs-gone-good-list |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250720163025/https://www.teenvogue.com/story/taylor-swift-tops-2015-celebs-gone-good-list |archive-date=July 20, 2025 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |magazine=[[Teen Vogue]]}}</ref> She received the Star of Compassion from the Tennessee Disaster Services and the Big Help Award from the [[Nickelodeon Kids' Choice Awards]] for her "dedication to helping others" and "inspiring others through action".<ref>{{cite web |last=Pacella |first=Megan |date=June 13, 2012 |title=Taylor Swift Receives Star of Compassion Award |url=http://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-star-of-compassion-award/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150713131701/http://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-star-of-compassion-award/ |archive-date=July 13, 2015 |access-date=November 27, 2015 |website=[[Taste of Country]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Cooper |first=Brittany Joy |date=March 27, 2012 |title=Taylor Swift to Receive 'Big' Honor From Michelle Obama at Kids' Choice Awards |url=http://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-kids-choice-awards-michelle-obama/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120712004900/http://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-kids-choice-awards-michelle-obama/ |archive-date=July 12, 2012 |access-date=August 30, 2012 |website=[[Taste of Country]]}}</ref> Especially early in her career, Swift donated to various relief funds following natural disasters. In 2009, she donated $100,000 to the Red Cross to help the victims of the [[Iowa flood of 2008]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Lee |first=Ken |date=August 9, 2009 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $100,000 to Victims of Iowa Flood |url=http://www.people.com/people/article/0,,20218079,00.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090607053519/http://www.people.com/people/article/0%2C%2C20218079%2C00.html |archive-date=June 7, 2009 |access-date=September 9, 2009 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]]}}</ref> The same year, she performed at Sydney's [[Sound Relief]] concert, which raised money for those impacted by bushfires and flooding.<ref>{{cite news |last=Moran |first=Jonathon |date=March 8, 2009 |title=Kylie to Play at Sound Relief with Coldplay, Midnight Oil |url=http://www.dailytelegraph.com.au/kylie-leads-mega-star-mercy-mission/story-e6freuy9-1111119064914 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140222112004/http://www.dailytelegraph.com.au/kylie-leads-mega-star-mercy-mission/story-e6freuy9-1111119064914 |archive-date=February 22, 2014 |access-date=December 30, 2009 |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph (Sydney)|The Daily Telegraph]]}}</ref> In 2011, Swift used a [[dress rehearsal]] of her Speak Now tour as a benefit concert for victims of [[2011 Super Outbreak|recent tornadoes]] in the US, raising more than $750,000.<ref>{{cite web |last=Sciarretto |first=Amy |date=May 23, 2011 |title=Taylor Swift's Speak Now ... Help Now Rehearsal Show Raises $750,000 |url=https://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-speak-now-help-now-show/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250822202707/https://tasteofcountry.com/taylor-swift-speak-now-help-now-show/ |archive-date=August 22, 2025 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |website=[[Taste of Country]]}}</ref> In response to the [[May 2010 Tennessee floods]], she donated $500,000.<ref>{{cite news |date=May 7, 2010 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $500,000 After Nashville Floods |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/10101914 |access-date=May 7, 2022 |agency=[[BBC News]] |archive-date=October 31, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251031081738/https://www.bbc.com/news/10101914 |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2009, Swift sang at the [[BBC]]'s [[Children in Need]] concert and raised [[pound sterling|£]]13,000 for the cause.{{sfn|Spencer|2010|p=65}} In 2016, she donated $1&nbsp;million to [[2016 Louisiana floods|Louisiana flood relief]] efforts and $100,000 to the Dolly Parton Fire Fund.<ref>{{cite news |date=August 17, 2016 |title=Taylor Swift Gives $1M to Help Louisiana Flood Relief Efforts |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2016/aug/17/taylor-swift-gives-1m-to-help-louisiana-flood-relief-efforts |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160817094148/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2016/aug/17/taylor-swift-gives-1m-to-help-louisiana-flood-relief-efforts |archive-date=August 17, 2016 |access-date=August 17, 2016 |newspaper=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Muhammad |first=Latifah |date=December 9, 2016 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $100,000 to Dolly Parton Fire Fund |url=http://www.etonline.com/news/204685_taylor_swift_donates_100_000_to_dolly_parton_fire_fund/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170113101939/http://www.etonline.com/news/204685_taylor_swift_donates_100_000_to_dolly_parton_fire_fund/ |archive-date=January 13, 2017 |access-date=January 11, 2017 |website=[[Entertainment Tonight]]}}</ref> Swift donated to [[food bank]]s after [[Hurricane Harvey]] struck [[Houston]] in 2017.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Blair |first=Olivia |date=September 4, 2019 |title=Taylor Swift Makes 'Very Sizeable Donation' To A Food Bank in Houston After Hurricane Harvey |url=https://www.elle.com/uk/life-and-culture/culture/news/a38288/taylor-swift-donation-houston-hurricane-harvey/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190702033644/https://www.elle.com/uk/life-and-culture/culture/news/a38288/taylor-swift-donation-houston-hurricane-harvey/ |archive-date=July 2, 2019 |access-date=July 3, 2019 |magazine=[[Elle (magazine)|Elle]]}}</ref> She donated $1&nbsp;million to [[2020 Nashville tornado outbreak|Tennessee tornado relief in 2020]] and [[December 2023 Tennessee tornado outbreak|again in 2023]],<ref>{{cite web |last=Asmelash |first=Leah |date=March 6, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $1 Million for Tennessee Tornado Relief |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2020/03/05/entertainment/taylor-swift-tornado-relief-trnd |access-date=April 26, 2026 |publisher=[[CNN]] |archive-date=December 8, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221208064724/https://edition.cnn.com/2020/03/05/entertainment/taylor-swift-tornado-relief-trnd/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Nicholoson |first=Jessica |date=December 12, 2023 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $1 Million to Tennessee Tornado Relief Fund |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-donates-one-million-tennessee-tornado-relief-fund-1235552015/ |access-date=April 26, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |archive-date=July 24, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724212208/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-donates-one-million-tennessee-tornado-relief-fund-1235552015/ |url-status=live}}</ref> as well as $5&nbsp;million to relief efforts after [[Hurricane Helene]] and [[Hurricane Milton]] in 2024.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Rosenbloom |first=Alli |date=October 9, 2024 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $5 Million Toward Relief Efforts in Wake of Hurricanes Milton and Helene |url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/09/entertainment/taylor-swift-donation-hurricane-relief/index.html |access-date=October 10, 2024 |publisher=[[CNN]] |archive-date=March 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260312173305/https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/09/entertainment/taylor-swift-donation-hurricane-relief/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

She has also donated to [[cancer research]]. As the recipient of the [[Academy of Country Music]]'s Entertainer of the Year in 2011, Swift donated $25,000 to [[St. Jude Children's Research Hospital]], Tennessee.<ref>{{cite magazine |date=June 15, 2011 |title=Big Gifts For Good Causes |last=Skates |first=Sarah |url=https://musicrow.com/2011/06/big-gifts-for-good-causes/ |access-date=February 22, 2026 |magazine=[[MusicRow]] |archive-date=February 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210185401/https://musicrow.com/2011/06/big-gifts-for-good-causes/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2012, she participated in the [[Stand Up to Cancer]] telethon, performing the charity single "[[Ronan (song)|Ronan]]", which she wrote in memory of a four-year-old boy who died of [[neuroblastoma]].<ref>{{cite magazine |date=September 8, 2012 |title=New and Hot Video: Taylor Swift Debuts 'Ronan' at Stand Up To Cancer Benefit |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/videos/taylor-swift-debuts-ronan-at-stand-up-to-cancer-benefit-20120908 |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120913054843/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/videos/taylor-swift-debuts-ronan-at-stand-up-to-cancer-benefit-20120908 |archive-date=September 13, 2012 |access-date=September 14, 2012 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> She has also donated $100,000 to the [[V Foundation for Cancer Research]]<ref>{{cite web |last=Knight |first=Joey |date=May 17, 2014 |title=Dick Vitale Holds Annual Fundraiser for Pediatric Cancer |url=https://www.tampabay.com/sports/basketball/college/dick-vitale-holds-annual-fundraiser-for-pediatric-cancer/2180291/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714222743/http://www.tampabay.com/sports/basketball/college/dick-vitale-holds-annual-fundraiser-for-pediatric-cancer/2180291 |archive-date=July 14, 2014 |access-date=July 30, 2014 |newspaper=[[Tampa Bay Times]]}}</ref> and $50,000 to the [[Children's Hospital of Philadelphia]].<ref>{{cite news |date=June 5, 2014 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $50K to Children's Cancer Hospital |url=https://www.azcentral.com/story/entertainment/people/2014/06/05/taylor-swift-donates-k-to-childrens-cancer-hospital/10034995/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210303025313/https://www.azcentral.com/story/entertainment/people/2014/06/05/taylor-swift-donates-k-to-childrens-cancer-hospital/10034995/ |archive-date=March 3, 2021 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |newspaper=[[The Arizona Republic]]}}</ref> She has made donations to her fans several times to help cover their medical or academic expenses.<ref>{{cite news |date=August 20, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift’s Cash Gift Helps Student Take Up Degree |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-53857694 |access-date=November 9, 2020 |agency=[[BBC News]] |archive-date=February 25, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260225133158/https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-53857694 |url-status=live }}</ref> During the COVID-19 pandemic, Swift donated to the [[World Health Organization]] and [[Feeding America]]<ref>{{cite web |last=Peppin |first=Hayley |date=March 24, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Responded to the Leaked 'Famous' Phone Call with Kanye West by Urging Fans to Instead Focus on Coronavirus Aid |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/taylor-swift-responds-leaked-call-kanye-west-urges-fans-coronavirus-donations-2020-3 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |website=[[Business Insider]] |archive-date=February 1, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260201133614/https://www.businessinsider.com/taylor-swift-responds-leaked-call-kanye-west-urges-fans-coronavirus-donations-2020-3 |url-status=live}}</ref> and supported independent record stores.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Grow |first=Kory |date=April 1, 2020 |title=How Taylor Swift Is Helping a Small Nashville Record Store Survive |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-grimeys-coronavirus-976063/ |url-access=limited |access-date=August 1, 2023 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |archive-date=February 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210164410/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-grimeys-coronavirus-976063/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Hissong |first=Samantha |date=August 20, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Starts Frenzy at Indie Record Stores With Surprise Signed ''Folklore'' CDs |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-folklore-signed-cds-indie-stores-1047417/ |url-access=limited |access-date=August 1, 2023 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |archive-date=February 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260212005243/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-folklore-signed-cds-indie-stores-1047417/ |url-status=live }}</ref> She performed "[[Soon You'll Get Better]]" on the ''[[Together at Home#Television special|One World: Together At Home]]'' television special, a [[benefit concert]] curated by [[Lady Gaga]] for [[Global Poverty Project#Global Citizen|Global Citizen]] to raise funds for the World Health Organization's [[COVID-19 Solidarity Response Fund]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Havens |first=Lyndsey |date=April 18, 2020 |title=Taylor Swift Sings Heart-Rending 'Soon You'll Get Better' During 'One World' Concert |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/one-taylor-swift-soon-youll-get-better-world-togher-at-home-concert-9361327/ |access-date=April 26, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |archive-date=April 24, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260424034841/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/one-taylor-swift-soon-youll-get-better-world-togher-at-home-concert-9361327/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Swift is a supporter of the arts. A benefactor of the [[Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame]],<ref>{{cite web |title=Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame |url=http://nashvillesongwritersfoundation.com/Site/about-us |access-date=July 2, 2020 |publisher=[[Nashville Songwriters Foundation]] |archive-date=March 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260309094153/http://nashvillesongwritersfoundation.com/Site/about-us |url-status=live }}</ref> she has donated $75,000 to Hendersonville High School to help refurbish its auditorium;<ref>{{cite news |date=September 23, 2010 |title=School Auditorium Named After Taylor Swift |url=https://www.deseret.com/2010/9/23/20142617/school-auditorium-named-after-taylor-swift/ |access-date=April 26, 2026 |newspaper=[[Deseret News]] |archive-date=April 26, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260426192754/https://www.deseret.com/2010/9/23/20142617/school-auditorium-named-after-taylor-swift/ |url-status=live }}</ref> $4&nbsp;million to the [[Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum]] in Nashville—the largest donation the museum had received from an artist—to establish the Taylor Swift Education Center, an exhibit and classroom space that opened in 2013;<ref>{{cite magazine |date=May 17, 2012 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $4 Million to Country Hall of Fame |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-donates-4-million-to-country-hall-of-fame-488365/ |access-date=April 25, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |agency=[[Associated Press]] |archive-date=August 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250806174721/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-donates-4-million-to-country-hall-of-fame-488365/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |date=October 12, 2013 |title=Taylor Swift Opens $4 Mil. Education Center at Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-opens-4-mil-education-center-at-country-5755418/ |access-date=April 25, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |agency=[[Associated Press]] |archive-date=May 8, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230508164237/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-opens-4-mil-education-center-at-country-5755418/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and $100,000 to the [[Nashville Symphony]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Ng |first=David |date=December 16, 2013 |title=Taylor Swift Donates $100,000 to Troubled Nashville Symphony |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment/arts/culture/la-et-cm-taylor-swift-nashville-symphony-20131216-story.html |access-date=April 26, 2026 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]] |archive-date=April 15, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160415120821/http://www.latimes.com/entertainment/arts/culture/la-et-cm-taylor-swift-nashville-symphony-20131216-story.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2012, Swift partnered with Chegg for Good to donate $10,000 to the music departments of six US colleges.<ref>{{cite web |last=Golden |first=Zara |date=October 1, 2012 |title=And The Taylor Swift VH1 Storytellers Contest Winner Is&nbsp;... Harvey Mudd College! |url=http://www.vh1.com/music/tuner/2012-10-01/taylor-swift-vh1-storytellers-harvey-mudd-college/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150712144643/http://www.vh1.com/music/tuner/2012-10-01/taylor-swift-vh1-storytellers-harvey-mudd-college/ |archive-date=July 12, 2015 |access-date=April 21, 2014 |publisher=[[VH1]]}}</ref>

